# Signing material. The production key must never enter the repository: anyone holding it
# can publish an update that existing installs will accept as genuine. Both conventional
# keystore extensions are listed, because matching only one is a trap.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
!debug.keystore
keystore.properties
# Base64 of the keystore, produced when loading the CI secret. This is the signing key in
# plain text — it must be deleted after use, and must never be committed if it lingers.
keystore.b64
*.b64

# Eclipse/VS Code Java tooling output
bin/
